---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CtaSection from '../components/CtaSection.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How I think"
  description="Deanna Glaze — product designer and player-coach working across AI, publishing, and digital health."
  theme="aurora"
>
  <section class="section--tight">
    <div class="container about">
      <div class="about__portrait">
        <img
          src="/images/about/workshop.jpg"
          alt="Deanna leading an audience-mapping workshop, smiling in front of a wall of grouped sticky notes"
          width="480"
          height="600"
          loading="eager"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="about__copy prose">
        <h1>How I think</h1>
        <p>
          <strong>I like understanding complicated systems made up of people.</strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          That's been the constant throughout my career. I've worked as a product designer, UX director, and design strategist, but those titles describe where I happened to sit, not how I think.
        </p>
        <p>
          I'm drawn to problems where tech, human behavior, business goals, and org constraints all intersect. Healthcare. Automotive. Publishing. Different industries, but the same kind of challenge: understanding how people, tech, incentives, and constraints interact before trying to improve them. I'm happiest when there isn't an obvious playbook and the work begins with understanding the ecosystem before designing a solution.
        </p>
        <p>
          My career hasn't followed a straight line. By design.
        </p>
        <p>
          The most interesting problems rarely arrive with the same title attached to them. Sometimes the greatest contribution I can make is designing an interaction model or helping uncover a viable product strategy. Other times it's building a design team, mentoring individuals, or helping an org rethink how product, design, and engineering work together.
        </p>
        <p>
          I've learned that leadership isn't tied to a title. I've found opportunities to lead from both IC and management roles. The impact changes, but the questions I ask don't.
        </p>
        <p><strong><em>What are people trying to accomplish?</em></strong></p>
        <p><strong><em>What's getting in their way?</em></strong></p>
        <p><strong><em>What motivates them?</em></strong></p>
        <p>
          Outside of product work, I explore those same questions through writing and books. I founded <a
            href="https://aerialbooks.com/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
          >Aerial Books</a> because reading has always been another way for me to understand people. Every novel, memoir, or work of history is an invitation to see the world through someone else's eyes. That curiosity has shaped not only how I read, but how I design, lead, and think.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaSection />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 2fr) minmax(0, 3fr);
    gap: var(--space-8);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .about__portrait img {
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .about {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .about__portrait img {
      max-width: 320px;
    }
  }
</style>
